    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1482-a1">

                <pb facs="1291" n="1033" xml:id="pg1033"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief Administrator for the German Governor General
                        in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Von Sandt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the American Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitlock</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 21, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In reply to your note of December
                        28,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1482-f1"/> I have the honor to state that the
                    Governor General has also exempted pharmaceutical products from all requisition
                    in the territory controlled by the General Government. I beg you to be kind
                    enough to so inform the Comité National de Secours et d’Alimentation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Administrator: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kaufmann</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
